  - TestFlight builds become unopenable

How to Renew:

  Method 1 (Recommended) - Renew via Xcode:
  1. Open Xcode → Settings → Accounts
  2. Select your team → Manage Certificates
  3. Click "+" → Apple Distribution
  4. Xcode creates and installs new certificate automatically

  Method 2 - Renew via web:
  1. Open your browser and navigate to developer.apple.com
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)
  2. Log in with your Apple Developer account
  3. Go to Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles → Certificates
  4. Click "+" to create a new Apple Distribution certificate
  5. Follow the CSR upload instructions

  Security Notes:
  Apple will NEVER:
  - Send you a "renewal code" or "device verification code" via email
  - Ask you to enter a code at appleid.apple.com from an email link
  - Redirect you to a non-apple.com domain for certificate renewal
  - Ask for your Apple ID password through an email link

  All certificate operations happen when you manually navigate to
  developer.apple.com in your browser. If you receive an email with
  a "renewal code" or "device verification code," it is a phishing
  attempt targeting Apple Developer accounts.

